I deep-read `prx0r/influence` through the latest push `88712bd` and compared it against the current OddHobb architecture, the new `pogpet/catalog/packs` gate system, and `prx0r/qprivately`.

The core idea is very strong. The implementation is currently more dangerous than it looks because **the documents describe a much stricter system than the code actually enforces**.

The best framing is:

> **qprivately = kernel**  
> **Influence = operating system / scheduler / control plane**  
> **Pogpet = product factory**  
> **product packs = immutable commercial truth**  
> **content factories = workers**  
> **Etsy/X/YouTube/etc. adapters = device drivers**  
> **the Influence middle canvas = human review terminal**

That separation would make the whole stack click.

