# So: should Etsy listings live in Product Packs?

**The product itself should. The Etsy listing should not.**

This distinction is important.

The Product Pack should answer:

> What are we definitely selling?

It should contain things like:

```text
SKU
product name
dimensions
material
price / approved pricing policy
personalisation options
supplier
production time
canonical product images
approved factual claims
audience
occasions
what it is NOT suitable for
physical sample status
```

Influence should answer:

> How are we presenting this product on Etsy today?

That includes:

```text
Etsy title
13 tags
taxonomy
image ordering
channel-formatted description
SEO experiments
promotion copy
listing ID
listing state
campaign attribution
live performance
```

Those change constantly.

Your product should not need a new manufacturing pack revision because:

> `"dog dad gift"` beat `"pet lover gift"` as an Etsy search tag.

That is marketing state.

