# There is an even more serious approval bug in Etsy

`etsy_listing.execute(task_id)` reads:

```text
title
instructions
done
```

Then uses regex to recover:

```text
SKU: ...
```

from the human-readable instructions.

That means the thing you approve is **not actually the immutable payload that executes**.

Then it recompiles the listing again.

That breaks the most important authority invariant:

> human approval must bind exact bytes.

Approval should never mean:

> I approve something roughly described by this prose and whatever the compiler produces later.

It must mean:

> I authorize payload hash `sha256:abcd...`.

